# Terraform local state and workspace files — never committed: state records resource
# details (IDs, IPs) that do not belong in a public repository, and .terraform/ is a cache.
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
# Note: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — it pins provider versions
# and belongs in the repo, same discipline as every other pin in this project.
# *.tfvars is ignored because it will carry the operator's admin_cidr and key name.
*.tfvars
# Chapter 18 stack secrets: the database password and the two EJBCA keys that protect the issuing CA's
# private key at rest. The template (.env.example) is committed; the filled file never is.
stack/.env
# Chapter 19 TLS material and database dumps: private keys (classical and ML-DSA), CSRs, and pg_dump output,
# which together with .env is the CA. Certificates that belong in the book go to transcripts/ by hand.
stack/certs/
stack/certs-stock/
stack/*.key
stack/*.csr
stack/*.dump
# JDK 25 experiment: the Temurin tarball lives in vendor/ (outside the repo) and is copied into the build
# context on the host; it never enters the repository. Its SHA-256 goes in the pins table.
stack/ejbca-jdk25/*.tar.gz
